<table id="featured" class="mainpagebox">
<tbody><tr>
<th>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Featured_article">Featured article</span></h2>
</th></tr>
<tr>
<td style="position:relative">
<div style="padding:3px 8px 2px">
<div style="margin-bottom:1.66em"><div class="mainpage-image-wrapper" style="float:left;clear:left;background:#fff;--darkbg:#222;border:1px solid #3B587E;margin:0 0.7em 0.2em 0">
<a href="/File:MTOboxart.jpg" class="image"><img alt="North American boxart for Mario Tennis Open" src="https://mario.wiki.gallery/images/thumb/7/7e/MTOboxart.jpg/120px-MTOboxart.jpg" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="120" height="107" srcset="https://mario.wiki.gallery/images/thumb/7/7e/MTOboxart.jpg/180px-MTOboxart.jpg 1.5x, https://mario.wiki.gallery/images/thumb/7/7e/MTOboxart.jpg/240px-MTOboxart.jpg 2x" data-file-width="1546" data-file-height="1376" /></a></div>
<i><b><a href="/Mario_Tennis_Open" title="Mario Tennis Open">Mario Tennis Open</a></b></i> is the sixth direct installment of the <i><a href="/Mario_Tennis_(series)" title="Mario Tennis (series)">Mario Tennis</a></i> series, released for the <a href="/Nintendo_3DS" title="Nintendo 3DS">Nintendo 3DS</a> in 2012 (and for other regions in 2013). The game includes some features new for the series, such as gyroscope support and supported online multiplayer (using the <a href="/Nintendo_Network" title="Nintendo Network">Nintendo Network</a> procedures before the service was terminated on April 8, 2024), though restricted only to the player's respective region. The game required 2019 blocks (258.4 MB) to download from the <a href="/Nintendo_eShop#Nintendo_3DS" title="Nintendo eShop">Nintendo eShop</a> until it was removed from the service after its discontinuation on March 27, 2023.</div>
<div class="noprint" style="float:right;position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;padding:0 17px 2px 0"><b><a href="/MarioWiki:Featured_articles" title="MarioWiki:Featured articles">More featured articles...</a></b></div>
</div>
</td></tr></tbody></table>
