<table id="news" class="mainpagebox">
<tbody><tr>
<th>
<h2><span id="Mario_&amp;_Nintendo_news"></span><span class="mw-headline" id="Mario_.26_Nintendo_news">Mario &amp; Nintendo news</span></h2>
</th></tr>
<tr>
<td>
<div style="padding:0 8px 1px 0;margin-top:-1px">
<div><div class="mainpage-image-wrapper" style="float:right;clear:right;background:#fff;--darkbg:#222;border:1px solid #3B587E;margin:0 0 0.2em 0.7em">
<a href="/File:Hello_Luigi_HOME_Menu_Icon_EN.jpg" class="image"><img alt="English HOME menu icon for the Nintendo Switch version of Hello, Luigi!" src="https://mario.wiki.gallery/images/thumb/2/2d/Hello_Luigi_HOME_Menu_Icon_EN.jpg/150px-Hello_Luigi_HOME_Menu_Icon_EN.jpg" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="150" height="150" srcset="https://mario.wiki.gallery/images/thumb/2/2d/Hello_Luigi_HOME_Menu_Icon_EN.jpg/225px-Hello_Luigi_HOME_Menu_Icon_EN.jpg 1.5x, https://mario.wiki.gallery/images/2/2d/Hello_Luigi_HOME_Menu_Icon_EN.jpg 2x" data-file-width="256" data-file-height="256" /></a></div>
<ul><li>The downloadable apps <i><b><a href="/Hello,_Luigi!" title="Hello, Luigi!">Hello, Luigi!</a></b> (pictured)</i> and <i><b><a href="/Hello,_Peach!" title="Hello, Peach!">Hello, Peach!</a></b></i> were released for <a href="/IOS" title="IOS">iOS</a> and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Android_(operating_system)" class="extiw" title="wikipedia:Android (operating system)">Android</a> devices on November 10, <a href="/2026" title="2026">2026</a>. Additionally, a new episode of <i><a href="/It%27s_Me,_Mario!_Stop_Motion_Shorts" title="It&#39;s Me, Mario! Stop Motion Shorts">It's Me, Mario! Stop Motion Shorts</a></i>, "<a href="/Toad_Can_Too" title="Toad Can Too">Toad Can Too</a>", was released.</li>
<li>Ver. 2.4.0 of <i><b><a href="/Super_Mario_Party_Jamboree" title="Super Mario Party Jamboree">Super Mario Party Jamboree</a></b></i> was released on November 9, 2026, which adds GameShare using GameChat for the <a href="/Super_Mario_Party_Jamboree_%E2%80%93_Nintendo_Switch_2_Edition_%2B_Jamboree_TV" title="Super Mario Party Jamboree – Nintendo Switch 2 Edition + Jamboree TV">Nintendo Switch 2 Edition of the game</a> and adds maps and rules as options for GameShare.</li>
<li><i><b><a href="/Minecraft" title="Minecraft">Minecraft</a></b></i> was released for the <a href="/Nintendo_Switch_2" title="Nintendo Switch 2">Nintendo Switch 2</a> on October 27, 2026, which updates the Super Mario Mash-Up Pack to support enhanced <a href="https://minecraft.wiki/w/Vibrant_Visuals" class="extiw" title="minecraftwiki:Vibrant Visuals">Vibrant Visuals</a> graphics.</li>
<li>The <b><a href="/Mario_Tennis_Fever_Open_October_2026" title="Mario Tennis Fever Open October 2026">Mario Tennis Fever Open October 2026</a></b> occurred on October 24, 2026 at 5:00 p.m. UTC.</li></ul></div>
</div>
</td></tr></tbody></table>
<table id="dyk" class="mainpagebox">
<tbody><tr>
<th>
<h2><span id="Did_you_know?"></span><span class="mw-headline" id="Did_you_know.3F">Did you know?</span></h2>
</th></tr>
<tr>
<td>
<div style="padding:0 8px 1px 0;margin-top:-2px">
<div><div class="mainpage-image-wrapper" style="float:right;clear:right;background:#fff;--darkbg:#222;border:1px solid #3B587E;margin:0 0 0.2em 0.7em">
<a href="/File:SM3DL_UScover.png" class="image"><img alt="The North American cover for Super Mario 3D Land" src="https://mario.wiki.gallery/images/thumb/1/13/SM3DL_UScover.png/150px-SM3DL_UScover.png" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="150" height="137" srcset="https://mario.wiki.gallery/images/thumb/1/13/SM3DL_UScover.png/225px-SM3DL_UScover.png 1.5x, https://mario.wiki.gallery/images/thumb/1/13/SM3DL_UScover.png/300px-SM3DL_UScover.png 2x" data-file-width="374" data-file-height="342" /></a></div>
<ul><li><i><b><a href="/Super_Mario_3D_Land" title="Super Mario 3D Land">Super Mario 3D Land</a></b></i> <i>(pictured)</i> is the only mainline 3D <i><a href="/Super_Mario_(series)" title="Super Mario (series)">Super Mario</a></i> game that is not playable on <a href="/Nintendo_Switch" title="Nintendo Switch">Nintendo Switch</a> and/or <a href="/Nintendo_Switch_2" title="Nintendo Switch 2">Nintendo Switch 2</a>.</li>
<li>In <i><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Casagrandes" class="extiw" title="wikipedia:The Casagrandes">The Casagrandes</a></i> graphic comic Friends and Family in "<a href="/List_of_references_in_publications#The_Casagrandes" title="List of references in publications">The Meet Up</a>", <b><a href="/Lulu" title="Lulu">Lulu</a></b> from <i><a href="/WarioWare" title="WarioWare">WarioWare</a></i> makes a non-speaking appearance when Carl is at the flea market.</li>
<li><b><a href="/Larry" title="Larry">Larry</a></b> is the only <a href="/Koopalings" title="Koopalings">Koopaling</a> who has never used <a href="/Warp_Pipe" title="Warp Pipe">Warp Pipes</a> in any of his boss battles.</li>
<li><b><a href="/Chuckorok" title="Chuckorok">Chuckoroks</a></b> from <i><a href="/Mario_%26_Luigi:_Superstar_Saga" title="Mario &amp; Luigi: Superstar Saga">Mario &amp; Luigi: Superstar Saga</a></i> take inspiration from <a href="https://zeldawiki.wiki/wiki/Octorok" class="extiw" title="zeldawiki:Octorok">Octoroks</a> from <i><a href="https://zeldawiki.wiki/wiki/The_Legend_of_Zelda_(Series)" class="extiw" title="zeldawiki:The Legend of Zelda (Series)">The Legend of Zelda</a></i> series, as both shoot rocks and have similar names.</li></ul></div>
</div>
</td></tr></tbody></table>
